From: kevin03L <kevin03L@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: tegra210: keep UART A clocked for the secure firmware

The first suspend after a boot of a Jetson Nano never came back, unless the kernel console stayed
awake (console_suspend=N); later suspends were fine. The L4T secure firmware (ATF) has its console on
UART A and prints once, at its first SC7 entry,

  ERROR:   BPMP not powered on

but the serial driver has just turned the UART's clock off for the suspend: the firmware waits for
ever for the transmitter. Keep the clock on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra210.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra210.c
@@ -3549,7 +3549,8 @@
 };
 
 static struct tegra_clk_init_table init_table[] __initdata = {
-	{ TEGRA210_CLK_UARTA, TEGRA210_CLK_PLL_P, 408000000, 0 },
+	/* The secure firmware's console: it prints on the way into SC7 */
+	{ TEGRA210_CLK_UARTA, TEGRA210_CLK_PLL_P, 408000000, 1 },
 	{ TEGRA210_CLK_UARTB, TEGRA210_CLK_PLL_P, 408000000, 0 },
 	{ TEGRA210_CLK_UARTC, TEGRA210_CLK_PLL_P, 408000000, 0 },
 	{ TEGRA210_CLK_UARTD, TEGRA210_CLK_PLL_P, 408000000, 0 },
